WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.331
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is yutori: room left over. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.824
Notice the weight of your body being held. Let the tongue rest and the shoulders fall. Allow this moment to ask nothing from you.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.149
Feel the quiet rhythm of breathing. When the mind moves ahead, come back to one simple inhale and one unhurried exhale.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:34.820
Yutori is margin kept on purpose: the time, space or energy you deliberately do not spend. Not what is left over at the end, but what you set aside first.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:01.449
A train timetable built with slack in it. The slack looks like waste until one train runs late, and then it is the only reason the day does not fall over.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:29.938
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.938
Let your breathing stay a little short of full. Not restricted, just unhurried. Notice that leaving room feels different from running out of it.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.217
For a little while, I will be quiet. Let thoughts pass like weather over a wide landscape. When attention wanders, return with patience.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.427
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:27.310
Keep some margin back today. Leave earlier than you need to. End one thing before you are empty. Let something be under-filled on purpose.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:53.124
Notice the sounds around you. Invite movement back into your hands and feet. Open your eyes softly. Thank you for meeting this day with Karma.
